{
"answer": "Brewing a cup of pour-over coffee requires attention to detail and a few simple steps, but with practice, you can achieve a rich and flavorful cup.",
"steps": [
  "Start by heating water to the ideal temperature for pour-over coffee, which is between 195°F and 205°F.",
  "Place a paper filter in the pour-over dripper and rinse it with hot water to remove any paper taste and preheat the dripper.",
  "Add one tablespoon of coarsely ground coffee for every six ounces of water, and gently pour the heated water over the grounds in a circular motion.",
