{
"answer": "Making homemade pizza dough is a simple process that requires only a few ingredients and some basic kitchen equipment.",
"steps": [
  "Start by combining 2 cups of warm water, 1 tablespoon of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of active dry yeast in a large mixing bowl. Let the mixture sit for 5-10 minutes, or until the yeast is activated and foamy.",
  "Add 3 cups of all-purpose flour, 1 teaspoon of salt, and 2 tablespoons of olive oil to the bowl. Mix the ingredients together until a shaggy dough forms.",
  "Knead the dough on a floured surface for 5-10 minutes, until it becomes smooth and elastic. You can also use a stand mixer with a dough hook attachment to knead the dough.",
  "Place the dough in a lightly oiled bowl, cover it with plastic wrap, and let it rise in a warm, draft-free place for 1-2 hours, or until it has doubled in size."
]
}

{
"answer": "To cook a perfect soft-boiled egg, place it in a single layer at the bottom of a saucepan, add enough cold water to cover the egg by about an inch, and bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 6-7 minutes.",
"steps": [
  "Start by placing the egg in a single layer at the bottom of a saucepan, making sure not to stack them on top of each other.",
  "Add enough cold water to the saucepan to cover the egg by about an inch. This will help the egg cook evenly and prevent it from cracking.",
  "Place the saucepan over high heat and bring the water to a boil. You'll know the water has reached a boil when you see big bubbles rising to the surface.",
  "Once the water is boiling, reduce the heat to a simmer (medium-low heat) and let the egg cook for 6-7 minutes. You can set a timer to ensure you don't overcook the egg."
]
}

{
"answer": "To prepare sushi rice at home, follow these steps: rinse the rice thoroughly, cook it with the right ratio of water, season it with rice vinegar and sugar, and let it cool to the right temperature.",
"steps": [
  "Rinse the Japanese short-grain rice thoroughly under cold running water for about 30 seconds to remove any impurities and excess starch.",
  "Combine the rinsed rice with the right amount of water (usually 1 cup of rice to 1 1/4 cups of water) in a medium saucepan and bring to a boil.",
  "Once boiling, reduce the heat to low, cover the saucepan with a tight-fitting lid, and simmer for 15-20 minutes or until the water has been absorbed and the rice is cooked.",
  "In a small bowl, whisk together 1/4 cup of rice vinegar, 1 tablespoon of sugar, and 1 teaspoon of salt. Once the rice has cooled slightly, pour the vinegar mixture evenly over the rice and gently fold it in with a wooden spoon to combine."
]
}

{
  "answer": "Here is a suggested three-day itinerary for visiting Kyoto, Japan: explore the city's iconic temples and gardens, immerse yourself in traditional Japanese culture, and indulge in delicious local cuisine.",
  "steps": [
