    "Day 2: Visit the Kiyomizu-dera Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage site and one of Kyoto's most famous landmarks. Afterward, stroll through the nearby Higashiyama district, known for its traditional Japanese shops and restaurants. In the evening, enjoy a traditional Kyoto-style dinner and watch a traditional Japanese dance performance.",
    "Day 3: Spend the morning exploring the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove, a serene and picturesque area with towering bamboo stalks. Then, visit the Tenryu-ji Temple, a beautiful Zen temple with a peaceful garden. End your day by taking a stroll along the Philosopher's Path, a scenic walking path lined with cherry blossom trees."
  ]
}

