{
"answer": "Performing simple stretching exercises can help reduce back pain by increasing flexibility and relieving tension in the muscles.",
"steps": [
  "Start by standing with your feet shoulder-width apart and your hands on a wall or door frame for support.",
  "Slowly lean forward, keeping your knees straight, until you feel a gentle stretch in your lower back. Hold for 30 seconds.",
  "Next, lie on your back with your knees bent and feet flat on the floor. Bring one knee towards your chest and hold onto your knee with your hand. Gently pull your knee towards your chest until you feel a stretch in your lower back. Hold for 30 seconds and repeat on the other side.",
  "Finally, sit on the floor with your legs straight out in front of you. Slowly lean forward, reaching for your toes, until you feel a stretch in your upper and middle back. Hold for 30 seconds."
]
}

